<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the generated iOS Info.plist. Tauri looks for `Info.ios.plist` beside
  tauri.conf.json, which is why this needs no config entry — and why it survives a re-run of
  `tauri ios init`, unlike an edit to gen/apple/project.yml or the plist that xcodegen writes
  from it.

  The two usage strings are the same promises the macOS Info.plist makes, for the same reasons:
  iOS refuses camera access to an app that declares no purpose, and CoreBluetooth reports
  `unauthorized` without the Bluetooth key — which btleplug then surfaces as "no cube found",
  a permission problem wearing a hardware problem's face. Deliberately NO
  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription: the scanner asks for `{ video: …, audio: false }`.

  THIS FILE IS THE ONE SOURCE OF BOTH STRINGS ON iOS (2026-09-05). They were also written into
  gen/apple/project.yml, in different words — the Bluetooth sentence there named no brand, this
  one named one — and only the non-shipping copy was tested. Tauri merges this file over the
  xcodegen output on every `tauri ios dev|build`, which is why the committed
  gen/apple/cubus-desktop_iOS/Info.plist carries THESE words and not project.yml's: the merge
  is what ships. project.yml no longer declares either key, and apps/web/test/mobile-shell.test.mjs
  reads this file and the committed plist and asserts they agree, brand-free.

  UISupportedInterfaceOrientations~iphone is stage-contract decision 6 — phones are portrait-
  locked, iPad rotates freely, so the generated all-orientations list stands for iPad and this
  narrows it for phones only. UIRequiresFullScreen is decision 7: Split View at 1/3 width is
  unsupported for now, and the portrait floor stays at the iPhone SE's 375px. That key is still
  honoured on iPadOS 26 and is deprecated for a later release; when Apple stops honouring it the
  contract's decision 7 is what gets revisited, not this file.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Cubus reads your cube's six sides through the camera. Everything happens on this device — no image is stored or sent anywhere.</string>
	<key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Cubus talks to your smart cube over Bluetooth, so it can follow the moves you make. It connects only to a cube you choose.</string>
	<key>UISupportedInterfaceOrientations~iphone</key>
	<array>
		<string>UIInterfaceOrientationPortrait</string>
	</array>
	<key>UIRequiresFullScreen</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
